From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OKO build <oko@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] build: provide a wordexp() fallback for libc without it

BlueZ parses its interactive console input with wordexp(3) in
src/shared/shell.c (shared by bluetoothctl, btmgmt, obexctl and the mesh
tools).  The arm-rockchip830 uClibc-ng toolchain used for the OKO rootfs
is built with __UCLIBC_HAS_WORDEXP__ disabled and has no <wordexp.h>, so
the client and tooling fail to build.

Add src/shared/wordexp.h with the subset BlueZ uses (white-space
splitting with quote grouping, WRDE_APPEND, wordfree) and point the
existing includes at it.  No globbing, parameter expansion or command
substitution is performed, which is what the BlueZ shell expects anyway
(it always passes WRDE_NOCMD and feeds in its own command strings).
WRDE_DOOFFS is rejected with WRDE_BADCHAR instead of silently returning
an array without the reserved slots.

